# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your EmailJS credentials so the contact
# form can email the business AND the sender, with no backend and no mailbox.
#
# Setup (free, ~5 min) at https://www.emailjs.com :
#   1. Add an Email Service (e.g. connect the Gmail account) -> copy its Service ID.
#   2. Create an Email Template. In the template settings:
#        To Email   : {{to_email}}     (this delivers to the business + the sender)
#        Reply To   : {{reply_to}}
#        Subject    : New enquiry from {{from_name}}
#        Content    : uses {{from_name}}, {{user_email}}, {{company}}, {{message}}
#      Copy the Template ID.
#   3. Account -> General -> copy your Public Key.
#   4. Add your deployed domain under Account -> Security -> Allowed origins.
#
# Leave these blank to run the form in "preview" mode (validates + clears,
# but doesn't actually send).
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
